    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "We can count in jumps. Counting by 2s, 5s or 10s is called skip counting.\nSkip counting by 10 from 100 goes 100, 110, 120, 130 and so on up to 200.\nSkip counting by 5 goes 100, 105, 110, 115 and so on.\nDraw a number line from 100 to 200 and mark the jumps with arrows.\nOn the snakes and ladders board, if you take the ladder from 13 you climb to a higher number. A snake slides you down to a lower number.\nTo find how far a snake slides, count back along the number line.\nSkip counting helps us add quickly and find patterns in numbers."
    }
